From d3a92ab729d04ebc075ae4417cde962448a76fff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ilya <ilunix@pc.ubuntu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:50:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] RDE: metafile: WMF/EMF text records (MathType formula
 previews)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WMF reader dropped all text records, so MathType/Equation preview metafiles
(which are pure text: Times New Roman / Symbol / MT Extra / Arial) rendered
as empty images — in RDE imported .docx formulas looked like blank spaces.

- read CreateFontIndirect/FontIndirect, TextOut/ExtTextOut (byte and 16-bit
  length forms), SetTextCharacterExtra, SetTextColor, SetBkColor,
  ExtTextOut options (ETO_OPAQUE/ETO_CLIPPED), Rectangle (opaque fill
  behind text), and WmfCanvas/EmfCanvas font+text state;
- truncate CREATEFONTINDIRECT face names at the first NUL (MathType pads
  names with junk after NUL, which broke font resolution);
- convert text bytes to Unicode per charset (ANSI/CP1252, CP1251, CP1250)
  and full Adobe Symbol encoding incl. bracket pieces 0xE6..0xFE ->
  U+239B..U+23AE; MT Extra 0x26 -> U+02D9 (dot above), oracle-checked
  against LibreOffice rendering of the same WMF previews;
- raster fallback (Font::charset) for canvases that need it.

Verified: 70 metafile tests (7 new: text records, charsets, Symbol pieces,
NUL-terminated faces, opaque ExtTextOut, advances), clippy -D warnings,
cargo fmt. Visual: all 15 formula preview pages of the real .docx match
LibreOffice when rendered by WordCraft (RDE vendor probe).
